WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.980
Hey, Natsu, what are you doing for Christmas?

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.230
You'll be going all-out, right?

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.160
Should I try to get a reservation 
at the Gold Tower?

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.610
Well, the club sure would appreciate it.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.450
But don't go beyond your means.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.910
I don't want to be outdone by the other girls.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.160
It's Christmas, after all.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.400
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.700
In that case, I'll take you up on your offer.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.460
All right!

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.460
Anyway, you two should go 
home and get some sleep.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.040
Aren't you working today?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.030
Aww...

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:35.720
Natsu, I can't tell if you're nice or actually cold.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.740
You're just noticing that now?

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.600
I'm generally not nice to other people.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.730
My younger brothers are an exception, though.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.560
There it is! Natsu's bragging 
about his little brothers again!

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.910
They're twin boys, right?

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.020
Show us some pictures next time.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.730
No way. It'd be a waste.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.900
Whatever, brother lover.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.210
Bye.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.520
Natsu-san!

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.570
If you're leaving, want to get 
breakfast on the way home?

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.350
I guess it's already noon, though.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.710
Sure, but I'm not paying for yours.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.170
What? Cheapskate!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.710
You make tons of money! It's not fair!

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.420
I need to save money so my 
little brothers can go to school.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.220
Next year, they'll be applying to college.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.870
It's so disappointing.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.830
I became a host because I wanted to be like you.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.490
You seem really comfortable with your life,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.910
you're obsessed with your brothers, 
you're cold to me...

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:31.010
That last one has nothing 
to do with anything, Ikuyoshi.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.480
Please don't call me by my real name!

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.050
Anyway, time sure flies.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:37.850
They're already applying to college?

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.490
How long did you say you've been working here?

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.620
Four years?

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.260
But you know,

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:49.100
working that second shift from dawn 
until noon really takes its toll.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.950
And I'll be in trouble if I don't 
start being nicer to my liver.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.050
Good grief...

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.130
That makes you sound like such an old man.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.130
It's disappointing.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.140
Why do customers always prefer a guy like you?

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.310
Is it your face?

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.280
Sorry, Iku. Something's come up.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.650
We'll get lunch another time.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.380
What?! Wait, is it a girl?

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.540
You're picking a girl over me?!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.240
A beautiful woman is better 
than lunch with a dude.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.290
Bye.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.160
You really are the quintessential host!

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.920
<i>I don't have a choice.</i>

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.940
<i>How else am I supposed to make money?</i>

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>Everything changed five summers ago.</i>

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.380
<i>That day, when I came to, 
I was lying in a hospital bed.</i>

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.930
<i>Apparently, I'd been unconscious for a month.</i>

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.940
<i>Only my younger brother, Aki, blamed me.</i>

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.630
<i>If they hadn't gone to the airport to pick me up,</i>

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.440
<i>they never would've gotten 
into that accident, he said.</i>

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.580
<i>But I didn't remember</i>

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.720
<i>a single thing that had happened that summer.</i>

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.520
You're late!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.510
Kashiwagi Law Office

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.010
Pardon, Ma'am,

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.260
but if you swing that law compendium 
around, you'll do some serious damage.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.980
This boy's a host now, right?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.150
It wouldn't do to damage his face, then.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.270
Actually, it's the book I'm worried about.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:02.720
Mikiko-san, I came directly from work...

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.920
I have something for you from Haruko.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.020
Huh?! From Mom?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.530
Come to think of it, you two are friends...

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.620
Haru's Secret Memories

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.620
My First Summer

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.620
An Exciting and Thrilling DVD

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.620
Warning: Only to be watched by Haru!!

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.230
Here.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.510
What the heck is this DVD?
The name sounds like a porno!

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:22.410
Haruko said it was something very important 
that you forgot to take with you.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.460
Ah, to be young.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.460
Haru,

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.800
you still don't remember going 
to Haruko's place five years ago?

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.850
Nope. Why?

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.410
If you never remember it,

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:40.360
I'd feel bad for that boy you made a promise to.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:41.620
What boy?

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.830
It doesn't matter if you've forgotten.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.290
A promise is a promise.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.180
I'm going to live here in Japan with you.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.420
Uh... Who are you?

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.000
His name is Ren.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.920
He arrived at Narita this morning.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:08.400
Haruko's been taking care of him 
until now, for various reasons,

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.680
but three months before they passed away,

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.680
the Kaidou family formally adopted him.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.430
Adopted him?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.630
In other words, Kaidou Haru, as the eldest 
son, you're responsible for his care.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.440
He's your little brother.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:27.440
<i>What? No one told me anything about this!</i>

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.200
Ma'am, are you sure?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.200
It doesn't matter what I think. 
It's what Ren wants.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.160
And Haruko asked me to make it happen.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:42.530
But it's apparently Ren-kun's first time 
both going to school and being in Japan.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.410
And Haru-kun has work.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.170
It'll be fine.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.450
Ren's been living with that weirdo, Haruko.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.140
He's bound to be tough.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.390
What's Haruko-san doing now?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:55.600
She's in Switzerland.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.210
She was once a brilliant physicist.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.520
She's gone back there to do research.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.480
How typical of one of your friends.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.530
They're all talented, but strange 
individuals, on a global scale.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.030
Are you trying to get fired?

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.530
Well, come on in.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.080
It looked shabby from the outside, 
but the inside doesn't disappoint, either.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:25.790
Cramped

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.590
Hey, don't underestimate 
the housing situation in Tokyo!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.790
If you don't like it, leave!

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.540
No. I'm not going back.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.950
I'm living here with you.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.300
You're the one who said you wanted to do that.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.010
Well...

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:41.020
Sorry, but I don't remember that at all.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.020
Oh, and take off your shoes.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:48.030
I heard that you don't remember me
because of the trauma from the accident.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.570
But what about Quark and Lepton?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.030
What? The dogs?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.840
You know them? And they're still alive?

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.430
No, they're dead.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.060
They died that summer, a month 
after you returned to Japan.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.580
They'd lived long enough,

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.860
but I heard you regained 
consciousness shortly after that.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.800
When I met you today, I knew

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.890
that they'd been protecting you.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.760
Is there more to this story?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.720
I just got off work.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.500
I'd like to take a bath and go to sleep.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.170
Yeah, now that you mention it...

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.340
You do stink.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:34.160
You smell like copious amounts 
of cigarettes and booze.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.990
<i>This little brat...</i>

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.920
Haru, what happened to your twin brothers?

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.440
They're with their maternal grandparents.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.250
Why aren't you living with them?

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.230
We're not related by blood.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:58.000
They said they'd only take in their 
grandsons, and rejected me.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.260
I understand how they feel, though.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.470
But how did my parents adopt you

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.770
from an orphanage in Canada?

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.270
Are you originally from Japan?

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.570
Well, I guess that doesn't matter.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:18.280
Anyway, how am I going to 
explain this to my brothers?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.000
Say I'm your brother.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.290
There's nothing else to say.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.590
That won't work!

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:26.290
Until I can get my head around this,

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.070
don't tell anyone!

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.100
Fine.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:32.800
Then what?

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.630
He said he was hungry, so...

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.430
My refrigerator's over there.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.380
It's pretty big.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.260
It's open 24 hours a day.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.430
You have to pay for your food, though.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.440
I have to pay, even though it's yours?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.690
That's how it works.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.650
Frog Wallet

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.150
Can I use Canadian dollars?

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.650
As if!

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.310
Don't open things!

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.010
Don't put it back!

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.700
Why did you get so much rice?!

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:04.860
This morning, he exploded 
an egg in the microwave...

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.630
Your brother sounds so cute!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.580
I can't breathe!

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.900
You're more worldly than you look, Natsu.

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.660
Natsu-san, excuse me.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:18.390
Asakura-sama is at table four.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.090
Got it.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.030
You heard him.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.550
See you later, ladies.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.220
What? You're leaving already?

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.320
I'll entertain you for the rest of your stay.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.930
It seems more like we'd be 
doing you a favor, Iku-chan.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.230
That's so mean!

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.530
Hey, we've been seeing her a lot lately.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:38.450
Asakura-sama is an office lady.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.820
She usually comes here on weekends...

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.570
But lately she's been coming on weekdays
too, now that you mention it.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:45.750
Oh, my.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.850
So she's an unaccustomed 
office lady who got hooked?

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.290
The watch...

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.000
Huh?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:57.090
You're not wearing it, even though 
I gave it to you the other day.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.130
Oh, sorry.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.240
I was nearly late to work today,

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:05.810
so I forgot to put on the watch, 
and all my other accesories.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.860
Things are chaotic at home right now.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.090
Because of your new little brother?

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:13.940
Huh? How do you know about that?

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.820
You were having such fun talking about it.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:19.450
Oh, sorry about that. Were we being loud?

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.830
A little.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:24.420
But you can't help it, with those 
girls as your customers.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.370
I know how you feel, though.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.160
I grew up without a father, 
and I have a younger sister.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.840
I feel like I have to work.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.340
You're a kind older sister 
who cares for her younger sister.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.800
What you're doing is admirable, too.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:44.350
You took in your little brother, right?

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.350
Not that little. He's about this big.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.970
The hard part is getting him into a school.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:52.850
I'm thinking of starting him next year, but...

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:55.690
I'll do it for you, then.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:57.980
Huh? But...

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:01.240
Your apartment is close to mine.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:02.710
Oh, uh...

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:05.380
Thanks, but I'm fine.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:09.240
My lawyer says she'll handle 
everything if I ask her to.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:13.050
Really? But lawyers are so expensive.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.750
It's a waste of money.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:17.980
<i>I don't deal well with customers like her.</i>

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:24.290
Ren?

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.470
What are you doing?

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:32.470
Don't scare me! I thought you were a grizzly bear!

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:36.540
Ren, you won't be attacked by any bears in Tokyo.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.480
Don't worry.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.830
You're lying!

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.940
Haruko said there were stray bears!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.140
That hag...

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.560
There are no bears in Tokyo.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.490
Anyway, what were you looking at?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.900
Manga?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.750
There weren't any at the library.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:57.270
Oh, yeah, they might be a good way to 
quickly learn about Japanese culture.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:58.750
Want me to buy you some?

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.500
Are you sure?

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.330
A few manga books are nothing.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.870
<i>Well, well.</i>

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:09.070
<i>So he can make expressions 
appropriate for his age.</i>

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:17.440
Ren,

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.640
go take a bath.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.440
I'll go buy dinner in the meantime.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:23.940
Haru...

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.490
What order am I supposed to read this in?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.950
Can't follow the panels

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.950
Huh?! Is this your first time reading manga?

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.420
I see...

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:34.350
Like this, huh?

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.180
Come to think of it, 
you're up pretty late today.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.460
Normally, you're asleep by now.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.930
I have the day off tomorrow.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:46.230
I finally get some time to relax.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.390
Now, go take your bath!

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.370
No, I'll take one later.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.600
Ren...

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.340
When was the last time you took a bath?

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:00.530
Be serious!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.550
It's been almost a week since you came to Japan!

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:04.990
That's gross! Take a bath!

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.260
No way!

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.740
The bath here is cramped, dark, and creepy!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.020
How rude!

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.600
It may be cramped, but it's just old!

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.500
And I'm enough of a neat freak to keep it clean!

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.250
If it's that scary, close your eyes.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.500
I'll give you a bath myself.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.260
I'm exhausted...

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.010
Huh?

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:33.640
<i>I feel like I've done this before...</i>

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.160
<i>But where?</i>

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.730
I'm hungry.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.270
Me, too.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.690
Let's go out to eat somewhere...

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.780
Bro! It's me, Aki!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:49.450
Shima's with me!

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.610
Bro, you've got tomorrow off, right?

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.240
Buy us dinner!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.660
<i>Why is this happening?</i>

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:00.610
Bro?

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:02.130
G-Give me a minute!

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.630
I just got out of the tub!

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.920
Ren, please.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.680
I still haven't told them about you.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.640
Um... And they've got exams coming up.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.390
Anyway, just stay in here until 
I say you can come out.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:17.940
Okay.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.890
Bro!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:22.680
What are you doing?

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.880
Aki, you'll bother the neighbors.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.890
That's enough.

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.400
Keep it down!

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.330
You should learn to be a little quieter...

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:33.990
Aki?

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.160
What, you really were taking a bath?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.000
So you don't have a woman in here.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.250
You shouldn't be here when you 
have exams to study for.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.940
But, Brother,

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:47.680
you haven't been answering your phone.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.510
We were worried.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.780
Bro, feed us some meat!

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.510
Huh?

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.120
I'm sick of old people food.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.020
It tastes like nothing, and it's all vegetables.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.590
Okay, okay!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.270
Kanada

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.530
Damn it...

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:11.740
They ate a ton of the good meat.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:15.200
Carry-out food

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:15.200
<i>How am I going to tell them, anyway?</i>

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:18.430
<i>I'd like to avoid causing a commotion right now.</i>

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:21.290
<i>I should at least wait 
until their exams are over.</i>

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.190
I'm home.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.970
Sorry I'm late.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.260
Ren? Are you asleep?

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.060
Huh?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.510
Just stay in here until 
I say you can come out.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.520
R-Ren?!

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:45.430
Re...

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.770
Can I come out now?

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.780
I'm asking if I can come out now.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.140
Y-Yeah...

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:59.200
Then I'm going to bed.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:02.200
Ren!

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:03.120
Hey...

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:09.090
I'm sorry, Ren. I'm so sorry.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:13.450
I won't trap you alone in there anymore.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.940
I wasn't trapped.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.100
You don't have to apologize.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.740
Still, I'm sorry.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.780
I mean... I was wrong.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.280
I'm sorry.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:30.960
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.280
<i>I feel like I'm about to cry...</i>

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.640
That was some good beef.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:44.250
Aki, there were shoes I didn't 
recognize in the apartment.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:44.960
Huh?

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.460
But I didn't smell a woman.

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.460
They weren't women's shoes,

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:51.950
but a child's.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:52.710
Huh?

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:56.130
That turd didn't have a kid, did he?!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.350
No, he's only 22.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.640
Besides, he knows how to 
handle that sort of thing.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.600
I guess he does, despite being our brother.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.290
Did you know Haruko-san went to Switzerland?

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:09.560
His mom?

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.640
Someone said they saw her 
at Narita the other day

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.980
with a boy a little younger than us.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:20.890
Where on earth do you get 
that kind of information?

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.830
You'd be curious, too, 
if you saw this family register.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:30.830
After the accident, when I left the hospital,

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:33.600
I stayed in a home for a while.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:37.590
There were six kids between age three 
and my age, living in one house.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:42.480
The employees took turns staying 
and taking care of us there.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:46.100
I was kicked out after about 
three months, though.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.450
Why?

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.060
Because I slept with one of
the female employees, I guess.

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.050
I was really lonely...

00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:00.400
My parents' funeral was over 
before I knew it was happening.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.600
My brother blamed me.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:05.370
But I didn't remember anything.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.150
I thought someone might have saved me,

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:13.210
but I tried to remember before bed 
every night, and I just couldn't.

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:15.880
Soon, I couldn't sleep at all anymore.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.850
I was lonely,

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:22.010
but being around people I knew made
me feel like they were blaming me.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.280
I stopped seeing my brothers.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.820
But I don't want to be alone.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:31.060
You have me.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:33.860
Even after you returned to Japan,

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:38.500
I wasn't alone, because of 
the promise you made to me.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.030
I could believe we were still connected.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:48.830
You're the only one who ever called me "family."

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.750
Ren, can I join you?

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:56.950
You're crowding me.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.710
I like it that way.

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:03.340
You kind of smell nice. Like a child's—

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.350
I'm not a child!

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:08.350
That's what you get mad about?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.040
<i>This kid crossed an ocean</i>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:12.530
Wait, I meant that it's a nostalgic 
smell that reminds me of my childhood!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.850
<i>carrying this "promise" that I had lost.</i>

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:13.850
Yeah, that's it!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.900
Move! Go sleep by yourself!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.530
<i>He doesn't care that I'm cold-hearted.</i>

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.790
Don't kick me out! It's cold!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:22.060
<i>Will I be able to make 
a new promise with him?</i>

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:20.840
Come on, Ren! Come on!

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:21.680
Shut up!

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:25.870
The zoo?

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:30.250
Since it's the neighborhood zoo, 
it's a bit small, but they've got elephants.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.320
Elephants?

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:34.390
There weren't any elephants in the Rockies.

00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:35.130
Wanna go?

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.130
Yeah!

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.640
Aren't you cold?

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:41.570
I'm fine.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:42.960
Is that Ren?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.730
Now, then...

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:48.180
Why don't you tell us exactly what's going on?

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:52.630
U-Um...

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:54.810
I'm taking care of this kid for a friend.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:57.520
Liar! We have proof!

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.770
Spit it out already!

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:01.690
Aw, jeez. What a pain in the butt...

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:05.170
That's right! He's my youngest brother, Kaidou Ren!

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:06.030
Got a problem with that?

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.900
Why are you snapping at us, you turd?

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:10.790
I'll never accept him!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:14.160
It doesn't matter if you don't! 
He's already on the register!

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.590
Mom and Dad made the decision! 
You should listen to your parents!

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:18.610
Shut up!

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.990
When I said I'd never accept him, I meant it!

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:22.490
What was that?!

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:24.700
It doesn't matter.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:29.730
I don't care if you accept me or not.

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:32.810
I just came to fulfill my promise with Haru.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:36.380
So you don't have to think of me as your brother.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:40.070
The only family I need is Haru.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.450
Ren...

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:42.480
Don't be stupid!

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:42.920
Huh?

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.700
He's our brother!

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.070
We won't let you take him!

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.180
That's not my problem.

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:49.710
I'm going to live with Haru.

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:50.960
What?!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.830
Uh, Aki? Ren?

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:58.910
My brothers are so embarrassing...

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.130
Next Time
